35,2,1,talk,May,,"It's worse than I thought. One house filed almost all the complaints, and some of our frontages are way too narrow for a bin.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The station block's bin house smells terrible in summer, and supervising the bins takes nearly an hour each time.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"A shelter is expensive! Even with a forty percent subsidy, we're looking at a lot of money, plus yearly costs for nets and deodorant.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The station block ended up fighting over a broken latch. Also, people admitted they wouldn't actually stop a neighbor from leaving bags late.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The paperwork for a permanent build is extensive, and the truck arrives so early that a strict window might wake us all up.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, if a shelter is too expensive, maybe rotating the location is fairer?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, but if some frontages are too narrow, rotating might just move the problem to a worse spot.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,Exactly. And the ledger shows we already spend money on things that aren't working.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"If we rotate or supervise, will that just lead to more arguments about who is doing it right?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,The filing for rotating sites is also a burden; each change needs a new notice to the ward.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if the bin house smells and the window is too tight, what's left?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"We need something that doesn't create a new nuisance. The ""supervised"" idea seems exhausting.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I can't support a permanent structure if it puts a huge financial strain on everyone.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that any ""rule"" we set will just be broken, leading to more tension.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must balance the physical burden with the administrative one.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
